:false,"id":"control-472-61","label":"Changer style","options":[{"disabled":false,"label":"Double arm","value":"double_arm"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Umbrella / shuttle","value":"umbrella"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Carousel / chain / wheel","value":"carousel_chain"},{"disabled":false,"label":"Other / custom","value":"other"}],"role":"select","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":"double_arm"},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-62","label":"Positioning before M6","options":[{"disabled":false,"label":"SUPA Z, then M6","value":"supa_z"},{"disabled":false,"label":"M6 / PLC owns motion","value":"controller_managed"},{"disabled":false,"label":"SUPA Z, fixed XY, M6","value":"supa_z_then_xy"}],"role":"select","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":"supa_z"},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-63","label":"SUPA retract Zmm (machine)","role":"number","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":"0"},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-64","label":"Tool edge Dindex","role":"number","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":"1"},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-65","label":"M1 between tools","role":"checkbox","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":false},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-66","label":"Allow next-tool T preload","role":"checkbox","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":false},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-67","label":"Manage custom posts in Settings…","role":"button","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog"},{"disabled":false,"expanded":false,"id":"control-472-68","label":"Legacy .nbpost source inspection","role":"button","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog"},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-69","label":"I reviewed the target, machine-specific post settings and offset assumptions. This is not machine safety certification.","role":"checkbox","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","value":false},{"disabled":false,"id":"control-472-70","label":"Cancel","role":"button","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog"},{"disabled":true,"id":"control-472-71","label":"Check & prepare NC","role":"button","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog"}],"name":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog","text":"Post NC — Setup 1 POST Siemens 828D · native · 3-axis Change machine in Setup… Program number Program name Sequence numbers Native Siemens: G1 engagement/cancellation with XY travel, NORM approach and explicit G451 intersection corners (outside turns up to 90°). Rounded leads are optional. Verify the machine-data corner-switch limit; Z-only startup and G450 transitions are not supported. In-control checks assume the full project tool radius is entered at the control, not a wear-only offset. No travel, holder, fixture, PLC or whole-machine collision verification is performed. TOOLS FROM PROJECT LIBRARY Tool calls Tool calls come directly from the project tool library. Edit numbers/names there; no separate mapping or per-tool confirmation is needed. Duplicate or unrepresentable calls are rejected. T1 · Baseline 6 mm end mill WORK OFFSETS This setup posts 1 part under G54 . Change the count by editing the setup (double-click it in the browser). SIEMENS 828D Changer style Positioning before M6 SUPA retract Z mm (machine) Tool edge D index M1 between tools Allow next-tool T preload Double-arm machines normally have a calibrated tool-change height and spindle orientation. This profile emits G0 SUPA Z0 D0 before later changes. Next-tool T preload is disabled, so every executable T call belongs to the M6 immediately following it. Physical style is informational; positioning and preload are separate explicit settings. The standard profile emits no custom spindle slowdown macro. LATER TOOL-CHANGE EXAMPLE · VERIFY, DO NOT COPY BLINDLY ; DOUBLE-ARM EXAMPLE - MACHINE MANUAL WINS M9 M5 G0 SUPA Z0 D0 D1 MSG (\"NEXT OPERATION\") T19 M6 D1 POST STORAGE & REFERENCES Manage custom posts in Settings… Import private profiles and reference sources in Settings. Select a saved native profile in Setup → Machine & Controller. Imported scripts are not executed. Legacy .nbpost source inspection I reviewed the target, machine-specific post settings and offset assumptions. This is not machine safety certification. Cancel Check & prepare NC"}],"unlabeled_controls":[{"id":"control-472-55","role":"button","surface":"dialogs/cam-post-dialog"}]}}
